<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thebe of Pherae</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thebe of Pherae was a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jason-of-pherae">Jason of Pherae</a> and the wife of Alexander, tyrant of Pherae in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a>. Around 358 BCE she plotted with her brothers to murder her husband, whose cruelty was notorious; according to ancient writers she hid his guards' weapons and let her brothers into his bedroom. Her brothers then ruled Pherae in turn until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a> intervened in Thessaly.</p></div>
